    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Upload naming — the name is normalised, not the link escaped",
      "prov:value": "> **Lives in `library-core`, not `folio-core`.** It was written into\n> `folio-core` on 2026-09-30 and moved the same day, when bean `9umr` carved\n> the library topic out: `library-core` is *\"acquisition, ingestion and\n> archiving of sources (arXiv, web pages, photos, uploads)\"*, and what an\n> ingested file may be CALLED is that topic's question. It sits beside\n> `uploads-watch` and `library-ingestion`, which is where somebody looking for\n> it will look.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 9umr",
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why those characters and not \"everything a slug would change\"",
      "prov:value": "**Case is not the defect.** A first draft normalised with `slugify` — lowercase,\nnon-alphanumeric to `-` — and reported **110** findings over\n`uploads/`/`library/`, of which **77** were `README.md` → `readme.md`. Renaming\n`README.md` breaks every link to it and every generator that writes one: a\ncheck damaging correct names to enforce a convention nobody asked for. Narrowed\nto the characters that actually break something, the same corpus reports **34**."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why those characters and not \"everything a slug would change\"",
      "prov:value": "| character | what it breaks |\n|---|---|\n| space, `(`, `)` | a Markdown link target **ends at the first `)`** |\n| `[` `]` | the label half of the link |\n| `<` `>` `\\|` | the angle-bracket link form, and tables |\n| `#` `?` | a fragment and a query to every URL parser |\n| `&` `%` quotes backtick | escaping in a shell, an href, or both |\n| `,` | nothing — included for the stub convention, on the owner's ruling |"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Why the NAME rather than the link",
      "prov:value": "whose target resolves to `PIIS2589750021000388 (2`. That reddened `main` through\n*\"over the real tree, every link in every generated README resolves\"*."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "pr",
      "cat-harness:section": "Both layers now exist, and that is the right answer",
      "prov:value": "**The escaping half landed on `main` the same day, from a sibling session**\n([#1639](https://github.com/litlfred/folio-assistant/pull/1639)): `linkTarget`\nin `bootstrap-tools/scripts/subgraph-readmes.ts` percent-encodes every segment\nof a destination — parentheses included, because an unbalanced one ends a\nCommonMark destination just as surely as a space — and `decodeLinkTarget` in\n`cat-harness-tools/scripts/check-subgraphs.ts` decodes before asking the filesystem.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1639",
        "pull/1639"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Both layers now exist, and that is the right answer",
      "prov:value": "This section argued against that route while it was hypothetical. It is not a\nreason to undo it. **The two layers answer different questions**, and neither\nsubsumes the other:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Both layers now exist, and that is the right answer",
      "prov:value": "Owner ruling, 2026-09-30: *\"rename files to normalize to stubs and downstream us\nis OK.\"* Downstream references are expected to churn; that is accepted, not\nworked around. The ruling is why this check exists — not main being red, which\nthe encoder had already fixed by the time it merged.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-30"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Both layers now exist, and that is the right answer",
      "prov:value": "**\"OK\" means repaired, not abandoned.** The 33 renames left dangling\nreferences in **30 hand-maintained files** — 26 carrying structured-data path\nfields and 4 carrying a path in code or prose — plus everything generated. The\ncounts below are from `git status` over the repair, not from recall:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Both layers now exist, and that is the right answer",
      "prov:value": "**One thing deliberately NOT changed:** `cat-harness/docs/wireframes/uploads/as-is.html`\nstill shows the old names in its table. It is a hand-authored wireframe, so\nwhat it depicts is a design decision rather than a rename consequence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "How big the rename actually was — findings are not paths",
      "prov:value": "**33 paths**, measured from `git diff --name-status -M` rather than re-derived:\n26 primaries and 7 `.extraction.json` sidecars; 23 under the root `uploads/`\ndirectory and 10 across four the IRIS replica captures."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "How big the rename actually was — findings are not paths",
      "prov:value": "**And the reference sweep must read the same map.** A first attempt piped\n`git diff --name-status -M` through `awk '{print $2}'`, whose default field\nsplitting breaks on the spaces *inside the very filenames being renamed* — so\nthe old-name list came out empty, the sweep matched nothing, and it reported no\ndangling references. That is `dh4f` committed by the instrument built to refuse\nit. `awk -F'\\t'` is the fix; the lesson is that a sweep which finds nothing\nmust be shown to have had something to look for."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/library/library-core/upload-naming.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "What this does NOT cover",
      "prov:value": "## It does not touch a name that has no unsafe character — measured the hard way"
    }
  ]
}
